{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543087-extinction-the-fate-of-mongrels-by-j-f-sambrano","id":1543087,"title":"Extinction: the Fate of Mongrels by J. F. Sambrano","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-03T23:26:25-07:00","id":1543087,"title":"Extinction: the Fate of Mongrels by J. F. Sambrano","content":"So Ex-WtA Writer J. F. Sambrano whose sepration from White wolf is less than pleasant to say the least has been work on his own WtA like project.<br /> <br /> <br /> Said project is a table top game centered around a race of werewolves called Mongrels and presumably they fight against extinction of they race and possibly life on earth.<br /> <br /> From what I've read on the free post about the game on his Patrion it seems that the Mongrels are pretty similar to the garous though with some differences there six Lineages instead of breeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> With Lineages being how a werewolf was created/turned rather than a wolves birth shape like in WtA. The six linages are Born-weeping (born to a werewolf parents), Clan-bound(Kinfolks?), Curse-wrought(magically turned into a werewolf), Pelt-thieves(Mongols version of the skin dancers), Spirit-crowned(a spirit turns some one into a werewolf?), and Wound-favored(possibly the classic Hollywood turn via bite). Do note that only Born-weeping and Curse-wrought given focuse in his post about and the rest are pure guess work.<br /> <br /> Talking about the posts here's all the links to the free post about the project:<br /> <br /> the mentioned linages <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-94786732\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-94786732</a><br /> <br /> Another post covers the wolves' patron sprites. (called Tutelars)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-93021373\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-93021373</a><br /> <br /> And the final free post covers the introductory section of the write-up for one of the major tribes (or Dynasties) of werewolves called The Echo Severed:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-echo-108333286\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-echo-108333286</a><br /> <br /> And finally there's a paid post called the Divine accord which seems to go into some deep lore of the Mongols:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-108334305?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_share\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/extin..._campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_sh are</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T15:43:23-07:00","id":1543124,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is the best choice for a title...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T16